#
# lazy.nvim writes `lazy-lock.json` itself, one line per plugin at
# two-space indent, and rewrites the whole file on every `:Lazy sync`,
# `:Lazy update` and `:Lazy restore`. prettier expands each of those
# objects across four lines, so formatting it means the next sync reverts
# the formatting, and not formatting it means the `JSON & YAML` CI job
# fails: two tools insisting on owning the same bytes.
#
# The generator wins, because it is the one that runs without being asked.
# Excluded here rather than through a `prettier.overrides` entry in
# `package.json`, since an override can change how a file is formatted but
# not whether it is.
#
lazy-lock.json
